WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
A desk, and papers start landing on it.

2
00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.580
A shorthand journal.

3
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:05.570
A letter.

4
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.730
A telegram.

5
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:07.790
A cutting.

6
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.160
A ship's log.

7
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.740
A wax cylinder.

8
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:15.320
Then a typewriter clatters, and
the pile becomes one typescript.

9
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:18.190
A note at the front makes a bold promise:

10
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.980
"All needless matters
have been eliminated".

11
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.090
But one slot stays empty.

12
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.580
The vampire never keeps a record.

13
00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.620
So why does Dracula never get a diary?

14
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:32.730
In this mission, you'll see how the novel
is built from many documents and many

15
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.120
writers, not one narrator.

16
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.420
You'll follow its four movements,
from Transylvania to the chase east.

17
00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:44.260
And you'll watch Mina typing the
record, where "dates are everything".

18
00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:48.280
Your mission: work out why
Dracula never gets a diary.
